# Jobs that run on a GitHub-hosted runner (ubuntu-24.04) instead of the self-hosted [self-hosted, cocreiamo-ci]:
# 'workflow-file job reason'. Only a job that is short (seconds), needs nothing beyond a read-only GITHUB_TOKEN, builds
# nothing, uses no cache and reaches no cluster or host. tests/hosted-runners.sh refuses any other hosted job, and any
# entry here whose job has a secret, an environment, or a write permission. The reason: GitHub has no job priority, so a
# seconds-long required check waited behind 15-minute jobs on the six self-hosted slots (19 runs queued on 2026-11-06).
pr-title.yml check required PR-title check, about 10 seconds, pull-requests read only
shared-rules.yml check required CLAUDE.md and vendored-scripts check, about 15 seconds, contents read only
